<title>GERMANY: German 1996 metals production detailed.</title>
<headline>German 1996 metals production detailed.</headline>
<dateline>ESCHBORN, Germany 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>German primary metals production in 1996 was steady to higher, monthly data from state statistics office Bundesamt fuer Wirtschaft (BAW) showed on Monday.</p>
<p>Only refined lead was sharply down on the year at 176,337 tonnes, off 25.1 percent, confirming a year-long trend.</p>
<p>The report gave the following details, in tonnes -</p>
<p> -- METALS OUTPUT	Dec 96   Jan/Dec 96	   pct change</p>
<p>								over Jan/Dec 95</p>
<p>primary aluminium     49,026     575,156		 +  0.0</p>
<p>electrolytic copper   49,754     588,524		 +  9.5</p>
<p>zinc			27,611     327,015		 +  1.4</p>
<p>refined lead	    10,125     176,337		 - 25.1</p>
<p>SEMI-FINISHED METALS   Dec 96   Jan/Dec 96	   pct change</p>
<p>							    over Jan/Dec 95</p>
<p> aluminium		 92,493   1,476,248		-  1.1</p>
<p> copper		    94,847   1,456,468		-  3.9</p>
<p> zinc			9,342     174,371		 +  5.5</p>
<p> lead			 2,472	45,702		- 15.5</p>
<p>nickel		     1,176	17,479		 +  3.9</p>
<p> METALS CASTINGS	Dec 96   Jan/Dec 96	   pct change</p>
<p>							     over Jan/Dec 95</p>
<p>aluminium		 30,981     475,443		+  2.4</p>
<p>copper		     4,142	71,419		- 15.0</p>
<p> zinc			3,928	62,487		-  8.3</p>
<p>lead			   389	 6,259		+ 40.7</p>
<p>Semis and castings figures include alloys. Nickel and tin castings data were not given.</p>
<p>--Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
</text>
